      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I would avoid using superglue, as it can trap bacteria and prevent the wound from 'breathing', potentially leading to more severe infections. Petroleum jelly might also be too thick and slow drying, allowing dirt and bacteria to accumulate. Instead, try applying a thin layer of petroleum jelly (or similar products like Bacitracin cream), sealing the area, but leave the bandage slightly open to allow for airflow and potential drainage.",
